Changelog: 16-10-2026 04:11:04

Added. The app installs shadPS4 0.20.0 (14-10-2026), the newest stable release, in place of 0.19.0: Install brings
it where 0.19.0 is installed. The zip is checked against the SHA-256 GitHub publishes for it and still holds the one
Shadps4-sdl.AppImage. shadPS4 0.20.0 keeps shadNet's settings in a Network section of config.json and no longer
reads them from General once that section is there, so the app reads and writes them in Network when config.json
has one, and in General as before when it has not (0.19.0, or a config 0.20.0 has not saved yet). The rest of what
the app relies on is unchanged from 0.19.0: shadNet's protocol 1 and its sign-in messages, the log lines the app
reads, the default server, the system modules shadPS4 needs and the game folder names.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 23:29:43

Release 0.1.6.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 22:51:19

Release 0.1.6.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 22:35:35

Game Mode shortcuts are named with the system first, "[PS4] Title" (owner, 15-10-2026), so Steam's menus, such as the
recent games in the tray icon's menu, tell a game apart from the same title on Steam or on another system. A shortcut
in Steam with another name than the app gives it now, as one from before, turns Update Game Mode on; the update
renames it, keeps its play time, and removes the artwork under its old Steam number (core's write_shortcuts).

Changelog: 15-10-2026 21:28:55

Extract PKG (owner's decision 15-10-2026): the standalone Bazzite pkgxtractor is absorbed into this app and dropped
from the suite. Extract PKG… in the third step, a .pkg dropped on the window, or a package given to the app
(bc250-shadps4-manager file.pkg, the menu entry's %f; a later launch hands it to the open window) opens its window as
a dialog: the SFO preview, the icon and pictures (save as wallpaper), Rename to CONTENT_ID, Extract, Preview Only,
Salvage Mode and the two Compare tools, with the standalone's workers and messages. The output starts in the last used
folder or else the first game folder, with a line saying whether it is a game folder, and the games are looked for
again after an extraction, so the game shows up in the list. The window does not close while an extraction runs. The
package code (pkg, crypto, keys, pkg_type, psf, compare, compare_delta, cli) is in bc250_shadps4_manager/pkgxtractor/
unchanged; the terminal extractor is ~/.local/bin/bc250-shadps4-pkg-cli. The log, crash marker and progress are
~/.local/share/bc250-shadps4-manager/pkgxtractor.*; the last used folders are in the app's settings, adopted once from
the standalone's. The app has its own venv now (~/.local/share/bc250-shadps4-manager/venv, PyQt6 and cryptography):
the installer leaves the suite's shared venv, which goes when no other app uses it, and removes an installed
standalone pkgxtractor (not its settings). The launcher runs in the folder it is started from, so a relative path
means what it says. Without cryptography (an install from before) Extract PKG says to install the app again. Tests:
the standalone's (package, crypto, PSF, CLI, compare, the window as the dialog) plus the game folders as output, the
adopted folders, no closing during an extraction, the crash marker, the main window's button, a dropped package, a
later package and the games found after an extraction; the installer test covers the own venv, both launchers in the
caller's folder and the standalone removed.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 18:58:07

A nightly channel (owner's decision 15-10-2026: shadPS4's nightly builds are mostly stable). The first step has a
Nightly builds box: ticked, Install downloads shadPS4's newest nightly (its rolling GitHub pre-release,
Pre-release-shadPS4-<date>-<commit>, the same zip with the same Shadps4-sdl.AppImage inside) and checks it against
the SHA-256 GitHub computed for that build (the asset's digest in the API), which proves the download is whole, not
that the build was tried on the board; the window says so, says when a newer nightly is out, and the newer-stable
notice stays on the stable channel. Unticked (the default), Install puts the tested stable release back; that flow
is unchanged. The channel is remembered in the settings.

